 For more information, refer to Chromium's [`BrowsingDataRemover` interface][browsing-data-remover].
 
+#### `ses.clearDataSince(since, options)`
+
+* `since` Number - A non-negative, finite integer Unix timestamp in milliseconds.
+* `options` Object
+  * `dataTypes` String[] - A non-empty list of data types to clear. Unknown types throw a `TypeError`.
+    * `backgroundFetch` - Background Fetch
+    * `cache` - Cache, including CacheStorage and shader cache
+    * `cookies` - Cookies
+    * `downloads` - Chromium downloads
+    * `fileSystems` - File Systems
+    * `indexedDB` - IndexedDB
+    * `localStorage` - Local Storage
+    * `serviceWorkers` - Service Workers
+  * `origins` String[] (optional) - Clear data for only these origins. Cannot be used with `excludeOrigins`.
+  * `excludeOrigins` String[] (optional) - Clear data except for these origins. Cannot be used with `origins`.
+  * `avoidClosingConnections` boolean (optional) - Skip deleting cookies that would close current network connections. Defaults to `false`.
+  * `originMatchingMode` String (optional) - Origin matching behavior.
+    * `third-parties-included` (default) - Match first-party origins and third-party top-level sites.
+    * `origin-in-all-contexts` - Match origins in all contexts.
+
+Returns `Promise<void>` - Resolves when the Chromium removal operations finish.
+Failures expose the same `failedDataTypes` field as `clearData()`.
+
+Clears the selected data from `since` through the maximum native time. Invalid
+arguments throw before any removal starts. `clearData()` retains its existing
+all-time behavior. This method is available only in this patched runtime.
+
+This uses Chromium's native removal granularity. Cookies are selected by creation
+time. Local storage is removed for a whole storage key based on its last modified
+time, and quota-managed data for whole modified buckets. Selecting local storage
+also clears matching session storage without a time filter. Clearing cache also
+invalidates auxiliary caches such as CORS preflight, resource and back-forward
+caches that cannot filter by time. Origin filtering of cookies uses registrable
+domains, as documented for `clearData()`.
+
